        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent**: Reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform, providing approve/reject/request-info recommendations with reasons for a human admin. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, while web sources can hold decisions back but never approve. Offline evals showed significant improvements: fraud approval rates dropped from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations (local 9B model), and fraud approved without human review fell from 27% to 0%. Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment, achieving 86% accuracy vs 71%, with only 1% of fraud cases approved autonomously vs 8%.\n\n2. **Organizer Support Agent**: Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup without human review, pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API. Status: coming soon.\n\n3. **Portfolio Agent**: An agent on his portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects in natural language. It's also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it. This is a personal project.",
            "toolCalls": [],
            "stopReason": "end_turn",
            "usage": {
              "inputTokens": 2650,
              "outputTokens": 241
            },
            "providerContent": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Alberto has built three AI agents:\n\n1. **Fraud Detection Agent**: Reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform, providing approve/reject/request-info recommendations with reasons for a human admin. It auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, while web sources can hold decisions back but never approve. Offline evals showed significant improvements: fraud approval rates dropped from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations (local 9B model), and fraud approved without human review fell from 27% to 0%. Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment, achieving 86% accuracy vs 71%, with only 1% of fraud cases approved autonomously vs 8%.\n\n2. **Organizer Support Agent**: Answers event organizers' questions about sales, payouts and setup without human review, pulling live data from PostgreSQL and the payments API. Status: coming soon.\n\n3. **Portfolio Agent**: An agent on his portfolio site that answers visitors' questions about his experience and projects in natural language. It's also exposed as an MCP server so external agents can query it. This is a personal project."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
